  "body": "A tool library file (`.camtools`) can't carry a tool's drawn holder body.\n\n**Where:** `parse_tool_library` (`crates/app/src/tool_library.rs:109`) goes through `project::tool_from_json` and `ToolDto::to_tool` (`crates/app/src/project/file.rs:462`). It returns a `Tool`, which has no body field (`crates/tools/src/tools.rs:137`), and export writes `body: None` (`file.rs:456`). A library tool can only carry the `holder_d`/`holder_len` cylinder.\n\n**Effect:** a library meant for one machine's holders (e.g. BT30 ER20, TTS ER20 from the built-in holder library) has to carry an envelope cylinder sized to the holder's largest diameter and length instead (e.g. Ø46 × 60 for BT30). That over-reports: an ER20 nut of Ø35 under a Ø46 flange reads as Ø46 all the way down. It's safe, but it gives false hits near walls, and the user must re-pick every tool's holder by hand.\n\n**Fix:** let `.camtools` entries carry the tool body (the drawn holder profile and the built-in holder's name), round-tripped exactly like a `.camproj` tool. An older file without it still loads.\n\n**Done means:** export then import of a tool with a built-in holder keeps its profile bit-identical; pinned.\n",
